## Phase 2: Engineering Contract Generation (W2)

> **Goal:** Generate the self-contained, version-specific Engineering Contract that the spec describes in §2–§19.

### Task 2.1 — Define Engineering Contract Schema

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| **New file** | `services/project-ai/app/contracts/engineering_contract.py` |
| **What to do** | Define a Pydantic model `EngineeringContract` with sections: Identity, Content, UBRC, ILS, LSNB, RSSB, Theme, Renderer, Composer, Schema, Tests, Acceptance Criteria, Prohibited Behaviors, Delivery Format |
| **Key fields** | `contract_hash`, `workflow_id`, `target_family`, `target_version`, `snapshot_hash`, `canonical_references`, `acceptance_criteria[]`, `prohibited_behaviors[]` |
| **Acceptance** | Contract can be serialized to JSON, hashed with SHA-256, and deserialized back identically |

### Task 2.2 — Build Contract Generator from Snapshot

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| **New file** | `services/project-ai/app/contracts/contract_generator.py` |
| **What to do** | Given a `RepositorySnapshot` + target family/version, derive the Engineering Contract by: (1) finding canonical reference implementations, (2) extracting their common patterns (UBRC, theme, renderer routing, Composer registry), (3) generating version-specific requirements |
| **Key logic** | Scan `snapshot.blocks.verified` for I1/C1/D1 patterns → extract common contract → add version-specific identity |
| **Acceptance** | For target `Introduction/I2`, generates a contract referencing I1 patterns with correct UBRC, theme, ILS, LSNB/RSSB, Composer, and prohibited behaviors |

### Task 2.3 — Engineering Contract API Endpoint

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| **File to modify** | `services/project-ai/app/api/` (add new router) |
| **Endpoint** | `GET /workflows/{workflow_id}/engineering-contract` |
| **What to do** | Returns the persisted Engineering Contract for a workflow. The handoff page already calls this endpoint (see line 53 of `external-ai-handoff/page.tsx`) |
| **Acceptance** | Frontend handoff page successfully loads and displays the real contract |

### Task 2.4 — Contract Generation on Workflow Creation

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| **File to modify** | `services/project-ai/app/workflows/` |
| **What to do** | When a user creates a workflow (selects family + version), automatically: (1) run snapshot, (2) generate Engineering Contract, (3) persist with hash |
| **Acceptance** | After workflow creation, the contract is immediately available at the API endpoint |

