## Phase 3: Candidate Intake Pipeline (W3)

> **Goal:** Implement the candidate upload → intake → hash → compare → classify → placement manifest pipeline.

### Task 3.1 — Candidate Intake Service

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| **Directory** | `services/project-ai/app/intake/` |
| **What to do** | Receive uploaded files, compute content hashes (SHA-256), classify each file (component, schema, renderer, registry, test), bind to target workflow |
| **Key logic** | File classification by extension + content analysis: `.tsx` → component, `.registry.ts` → registry entry, `.test.tsx` → test |
| **Acceptance** | Uploading a set of files returns `CandidateResponse` with per-file hashes and classifications |

### Task 3.2 — Canonical Comparison Engine

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| **New file** | `services/project-ai/app/intake/canonical_comparison.py` |
| **What to do** | Compare candidate files against the Engineering Contract requirements: (1) Does it have UBRC? (2) Does it use `theme.primary/secondary`? (3) Does it have version routing? (4) Does it import ILS? (5) Does it hardcode brand? |
| **Key checks** | Parse candidate `.tsx` files for `data-block-id`, `data-block-type`, `data-block-version` attributes; scan for ILS imports; scan for hardcoded hex colors |
| **Acceptance** | For a correct candidate: all checks PASS. For a candidate with hardcoded SUIA colors: FAIL on brand check |

### Task 3.3 — Placement Manifest Generator

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| **New file** | `services/project-ai/app/placement/manifest_generator.py` |
| **What to do** | For each classified candidate file, determine the canonical repository destination: component → `packages/ui/src/tutorial/blocks/`, registry → `apps/skillhubcore-admin/src/.../registry/entries/`, types → `packages/types/src/` |
| **Output** | `PlacementManifest` with `{source_file, destination_path, action: ADD|UPDATE|EXTEND}` per artifact |
| **Acceptance** | For `ObjectiveO1Block.tsx`, generates destination `packages/ui/src/tutorial/blocks/ObjectiveO1Block.tsx` with action `ADD` |

